    {
      "id": "p0195-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The fact that there are so many different·versions of Undertale means that there are multiple English scripts that need to be managed, organized, and actively maintained. This holds true on the Japanese side of things too, meaning that Toby and 8-4 currently have to keep track of ten or so versions of the game. Understandably, this is a level of support not offered by most generic translation companies.",
        "raw": "The fact that there are so many different·versions of Undertale means that\nthere are multiple English scripts that need to be managed, organized, and\nactively maintained. This holds true on the Japanese side of things too,\nmeaning that Toby and 8-4 currently have to keep track of ten or so versions of\nthe game. Understandably, this is a level of support not offered by most generic\ntranslation companies.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09092828,
          0.32106429,
          0.69625638,
          0.42522143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08805216,
          0.32035,
          0.70159195,
          0.42629286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          24,
          25,
          26,
          27,
          28,
          29
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "《Undertale》版本众多，就意味着有好几套英语剧本需要管理、整理并持续维护。日语这边也是如此，所以 Toby 和 8-4 目前得同时照管大约十个版本。可以想见，一般翻译公司大多不会提供这种程度的支持。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 1,
            "end": 10,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
